### dual-sb HTTP request samples (REST Client / editor .http format)
### Start: ./target/release/dual-sb serve --dir ./mystore --addr 127.0.0.1:8080
@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080

### health
GET {{base}}/health

### put name=alice  -> committed generation 1
POST {{base}}/kv/put
Content-Type: application/json

{"key":"name","value":"alice"}

### put city=paris  -> generation 2
POST {{base}}/kv/put
Content-Type: application/json

{"key":"city","value":"paris"}

### overwrite name=bob -> generation 3
POST {{base}}/kv/put
Content-Type: application/json

{"key":"name","value":"bob"}

### read one key
GET {{base}}/kv/get?key=name

### list everything (generation, data_len, entries)
GET {{base}}/kv

### delete city -> generation 4
POST {{base}}/kv/delete
Content-Type: application/json

{"key":"city"}

### delete via query string (same effect, alternative form)
POST {{base}}/kv/delete?key=name

### missing key -> HTTP 404 {"error":"key not found"}
GET {{base}}/kv/get?key=ghost

### ---- crash-injection demos (in-memory; do NOT touch ./mystore) ----

### full matrix: crash during commit 3 at 8 points x 3 torn variants
GET {{base}}/demo/matrix

### first rollback: crash during commit 2, half-page torn
GET {{base}}/demo/matrix2

### single crash point: data fully synced, new root page torn in half
POST {{base}}/demo/crash
Content-Type: application/json

{"point":"RootWriteEnd","torn":"Half","round":3}

### crash before the data fsync, nothing survives
POST {{base}}/demo/crash
Content-Type: application/json

{"point":"DataWriteEnd","torn":"None","round":3}

### crash after the final root barrier: commit survives
POST {{base}}/demo/crash
Content-Type: application/json

{"point":"RootSyncEnd","torn":"None","round":3}

### three named acceptance scenarios with detailed reports
GET {{base}}/demo/scenarios
